course: dictionary
lesson: 14665
title: Coming before the main part
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Preliminary is built from pre-, which means before. Something preliminary comes first, before the main part, and it gets you ready for what follows. «The team won their preliminary round, so they are going to the final.» The preliminary round is the first stage, and the final comes after it.
explain: Scientists use the word too. «Before the big experiment, the scientist ran a preliminary test with three plants.» A preliminary test is a small first trial. Its results are not the final answer, so they are called «preliminary results». Ask yourself: is this the first try, or the last one?
explain: Watch for the formal use. «The meeting began without preliminaries, so we got straight to the vote.» Preliminaries are the greetings and small first matters before the main business. When you meet a word like this, look for clues about what comes first and what comes later.
fact: Preliminary means coming before the main part and getting ready for it.
fact: A preliminary is a first step or early round, such as a heat in a competition.
fact: Pre- means before, so a clue to preliminary is that the main event comes after it.
fact: «Preliminary» can describe results, findings or tests that are not yet the final answer.
fact: Preliminaries (formal) are things done before the main business, such as greetings.
exercise: «The school held a preliminary round of the spelling bee before the final.» What is a preliminary round? | A round for parents only | The last round, with the prize | *The first round, before the final
exercise: Maya says, «This is the preliminary report, so the final one comes next.» What does preliminary suggest? | Something that is finished and perfect | *Something early that is not the final version | A report written in a foreign language
exercise: «Before the talks, the leaders shared a few preliminaries, like hello and thank you.» Which word means the greetings and first steps before the main talks? | leaders | talks | shared | *preliminaries
test: «The preliminary results showed the new plant grew fastest in sunlight.» What does preliminary mean here? | Final results that are certain | Results about the weather | *Early results, not yet the final answer
test: Which word means the first round, before the final? | final | prize | *preliminary | champion
exam: «Without preliminaries, the judge read out the first name at once.» What does preliminaries mean? | A kind of sport | *Things done before the main business, such as greetings | The final prize | The judge's own name
